maria (Marketing PM): Quick sync — experiment plan for the pricing & packaging page. Focus: pricing calculator microcopy + FAQ refresh + inbound routing tweaks. Goal: reduce 'contact sales' clicks by 15% and increase ARR-qualified demos by 20%.
josh (Growth): Sounds good. Are we testing tier names, price thresholds, and CTAs all at once or in separate experiments?
maria (Marketing PM): Split into two parallel tests to keep signal: 1) tier-name + microcopy variants; 2) CTA wording + calculator UX. Routing change will be toggled for the same cohort as a secondary dimension.
izaac (Design): I'll build mocks for three tier-name variants today. Proposed sets: Variant A: "Starter / Scale / Enterprise"; Variant B: "Launch / Team / Business"; Variant C: personality-led like "Hobbyist / Builder / Partner". Also mock the calculator: inline examples, fewer inputs.
hana (Sales Ops): For routing: HubSpot mapping rule. Proposal: estimated_commit_monthly_usd > 20000 => AE queue, lead_status=MQL, else SDR nurture. Also add a webinar nurture path for medium-intent leads.
hana (Sales Ops): Example pseudo-config:
```
// HubSpot workflow rule
if (form_source == "pricing_calc" && estimated_commit_monthly_usd > 20000) {
  owner = "AE Pool";
  lifecycle_stage = "MQL";
} else if (form_source == "pricing_calc" && intent_score > 6) {
  enroll_in_workflow("webinar_nurture_v1");
} else {
  owner = "Inbound SDR";
}
```
josh (Growth): Let's use 'committed_monthly_usd' as the property name (less ambiguous). Also add a variant where we classify by 'projected_tokens_month' to capture volume-heavy users.
analytics-bot: Experiment created: pricing_pack_v3_abtest. Tracking keys: ga_event=pricing_calc_use, ab_test_id=pricing_pack_v3, hubspot_form=pricing_calc_v3. Sample target: 5k uniques per variant.
maria (Marketing PM): FAQ updates: add a short Q about "How upgrades/rollouts are handled" and "Difference between Dedicated and Private". Keep answers 1–2 lines plus a link to docs. Leo, can you draft?
leo (Content): On it. Drafting microcopy now — will keep it <150 chars per Q. Example Q/A: "Do you charge per token?" -> "Usage billed monthly by token rate; see calculator for estimates." Will post in thread.
